{"about_the_game":"<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Echo of Humanity is an atmospheric horror experience about silence, memory, and the remnants of what was once called life.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You wake up in a place that feels familiar, yet impossibly distant.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The corridors stretch endlessly. Lights hum softly. Machines still work, though no one is left to command them.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There are no enemies to fight. No puzzles to solve.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Only the unsettling calm of a world that has moved on - and the faint echo of something deeply human, still resonating in the void.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Echo of Humanity is less about survival, and more about understanding.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As you explore, the environment itself begins to tell its story, through architecture, through sound, through absence.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A quiet descent into the spaces between existence and oblivion.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>FEATURES</strong></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83e\ude90 Deeply immersive atmosphere of isolation and decay</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udd0a Realistic sound design that changes with each environment</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udeaa Liminal architecture evoking unease and nostalgia</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udcd3 Narrative told through space, not exposition</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >\ud83d\udc80 A slow, reflective horror experience with no jump scares</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Echo of Humanity invites you to wander, to listen, and to feel.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Not everything that\u2019s gone is truly silent.</p>","background":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/4099740?t=1774253162","background_raw":"https://store.akamai.steamstatic.com/images/storepagebackground/app/4099740?t=1774253162","capsule_image":"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/4